  "description": "KADCIF crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C40 H39 Cl2 Er3 N6 O12 2+,C1 H4 O1,3(H2 O1),2(Cl1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 3 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.506-3.538 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.21-98.39°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C41H49Cl4Er3N6O16. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
